  "term": "basal nucleus of Meynert",
  "definition": "The basal nucleus of Meynert is a group of nerve cells in the substantia innominata that sends widespread connections to the neocortex and is notable for high acetylcholine-related activity. It degenerates in Parkinson disease and Alzheimer disease.",
